WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.100
A defensive model for wormable prompt injection has four core pieces:
replication, payload, propagation, and persistence.

2
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:15.300
Replication means the malicious influence is copied or restated in a form
another model-enabled system may process.

3
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:24.660
Payload means the influence tries to cause an unwanted result, such as
changing content, steering a decision, using a tool improperly, or exposing
information.

4
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:31.060
Propagation is the path to the next surface. Persistence is how the
influence remains available for future runs.

5
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:38.580
This model is useful because it avoids mysticism. A prompt does not spread
by itself. It spreads only if the application gives it a route.

6
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:45.380
A summarizer may copy instructions into a generated summary. A retrieval
system may store poisoned text in an index.

7
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:53.780
An email assistant may include tainted content in a reply. A workflow tool
may write model-generated notes into a shared ticket that another agent
later reads.

8
00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.780
The blast radius depends on authority.

9
00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:07.460
A read-only summarizer with no memory and no outbound connector has less
propagation potential than an agent that can write documents, send messages,
modify tickets, update knowledge bases, or call business APIs.

10
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.700
The more systems the agent can touch, the more important permission
boundaries become.

11
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.180
Persistence is especially important.

12
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:28.420
If untrusted content is stored in long-lived memory, embedded into a
retrieval corpus, copied into templates, or synchronized into shared
records, the risk becomes less like a single bad response and more like
contamination of the work environment.

13
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.620
The same content can be rediscovered later under a different user, task, or
context.

14
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:42.420
Defenders should therefore ask which part of the chain they can break.
Prevent replication into authoritative outputs. Block payload effects with
policy and approval gates.

15
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:51.620
Limit propagation with egress and connector controls. Reduce persistence by
quarantining untrusted content and cleaning poisoned indexes or memory
stores.
